WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.660
I really am the strongest!

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.380
Good luck, Miss Emi!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.270
Card Capital's shop tournament 
is a great success!

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.740
If we always had this many people here, 
running the shop would be a breeze, right, Shin?

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.950
You mean "Manager", right?

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.450
And they're "customers"!

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.640
The most important thing is that everyone 
is smiling, having a good time.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.290
That's pouring it on a little thick.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.520
Manager...

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.730
Brother Aichi, Miss Emi won again!

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.160
Sounds like she's really trying hard.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.730
It's not about trying hard!

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.000
She's in the top group of 
winners in the junior division!

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.520
Apparently she did her homework, 
focusing on cute and strong units.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.690
I think we'd better take her seriously.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:48.560
I see! Then it's even possible 
that Miss Emi could join Q4!

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.040
We're finally on the same team, huh?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.950
Uh huh! That's the whole reason 
I wanted to get stronger!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.490
Are you okay, Kamui the Great?

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.010
OK, yo?!

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:11.800
For now, <i>he's</i> the top player 
in the senior division.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.820
Morikawa?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.370
Yes. I'm tabulating the results 
right now, and according to this...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.260
Sub-manager!

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.740
I mean... Manager... please!

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:29.210
It's unbelievable! I mean, Lose-umi...?!

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.150
Well, he really was strong. Even though 
he wasn't using his own deck...

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.470
Manager! Is that really a 
normal constructed deck?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.540
Yes, it's an uncustomized 
Golden Mechanical Soldier deck.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.970
Amazing...

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.710
Well, Q4 members...

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.400
Although Kai isn't here...

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:54.520
I don't mind you having a good 
time at today's shop tournament...

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.730
...but you've got the national 
tournament finals coming up.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.760
And so we have this!

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.880
"Awakening of Twin Blades" booster packs?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.000
Encountering new cards 
will make you stronger.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.340
So we'll reconstruct our decks!

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:18.990
Right!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.780
Songstress of the Sea

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.710
The national tournament finals...

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.970
Our opponents there will probably be 
stronger than anyone we've faced before.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.350
If we keep winning, we'll fight Caesar...

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.200
...and then AL4...

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.690
They're totally strong!

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.810
But I swear I'll beat 'em!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.370
Asaka Narumi, I haven't lost much recently.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.870
Next time, I'm gonna win!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:09.970
Ren...

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:14.210
All I was focusing on was winning,

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.720
which made the power of 
Psyqualia attractive to me.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:22.030
But I came to my senses...

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.820
...and remembered how fun Vanguard is.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.640
Since it's fun, you can compete with your 
friends and improve your techniques.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.210
You can get to know your rivals.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.670
I'm going to have fun playing Vanguard.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:40.020
I'm aiming to win, but 
while having a good time.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.480
Together with my friends...

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.270
That's how I will fight, Ren.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:58.580
Attack, Asura Kaiser! Finishing hold!

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.720
6 points of damage!

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.830
I won!

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.960
There you go! Just keep 
it up and you'll KW, yo!

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.700
Yep! Keep winning!

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.880
Junior Proof of Victory

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.370
I attack with Top Idol, Pacifica!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.600
I lost!

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.470
You did it! Emi, you're doing great!

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.780
Junior Proof of Victory

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.980
That's really impressive! Right now, 
I think you've got the most wins.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:28.640
Really?

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.220
Hey!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.930
Don't you think Miss Emi is a good fighter?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.600
I attack with my Vanguard!

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.290
I guard with Shining Lady!

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.480
Yeah, GF!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.660
And first to last, she fights 
the way she wants to.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.720
On top of that, it looks like she's having 
a great time while she's fighting, you know?

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.070
I attack with tinkling, 
twinkling Gold Rutile!

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.510
Another huge win!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.510
I attack with G-G-G-G-Gold Rutile!

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.160
Overwhelming victory for me!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.780
Senior Proof of Victory

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.080
Morikawa hasn't been defeated yet...

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:18.380
Card Capital Shop Tournament

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.380
He's out of control...

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.550
The strongest fighter, Katsumi Morikawa!

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:25.570
If you think you can beat 
me, give it your best shot!

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.700
Morikawa is amazing, huh?

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:28.990
Are you serious?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.370
I'm the strongest!

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.860
No, you're not! I'm the strongest!

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:36.750
Who said that?!

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.800
I remember you! "<i>Attack!</i>"

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.670
That's <i>not</i> my name!

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.090
My name is Osamu Kishida!

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:46.900
Is that right?

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:48.880
Do your best, Big Brother!

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.650
If you're going to call yourself "the 
strongest", please do it after defeating me.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.630
You think you're a match for me?

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:59.600
Of course, <i>Lose-umi</i>.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:01.440
Fine.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.860
You're ignoring that?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.550
Seriously?! He didn't react to "Lose-umi"?!

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.870
I never thought this day would come!

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:10.870
Against Lose-umi?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:18.630
Let me tell you something. Aichi Sendou, who 
progressed to the national tournament finals,

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.340
is my number one pupil!

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.360
I'm... what?

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:30.290
Because <i>I</i> willingly gave up my spot 
to him at a previous shop tournament,

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.700
Aichi Sendou is where he is today!

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.810
"Willingly"...?

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:41.530
I raised Aichi!

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:46.030
He became strong because I tested him!

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.370
I'm the strongest.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.300
That's <i>me</i>!

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.570
Now, now, both of you.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:59.010
Work off all that rage during the fight.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.050
Leave the grudge behind 
and just have fun, okay?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:05.400
Yeah! We don't need <i>two</i> strongest!

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.940
I'll show you that I'm the number 
one, ultra-special, deluxe,

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.540
wonderful, beautiful, grateful, 
delicious, strongest of all!

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.970
In that case, I'll prove that I'm the 
very eccentric, best, strong, ultimate,

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.000
congratulation, natural, 
fantastic, strongest...

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.550
...of them all!

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.200
That doesn't even make sense!

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:22.980
Look who's talking!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.440
Enough! Showdown time!

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.370
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.740
Okay. Let's let them do their 
thing, while we do ours...

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.320
Guess I didn't have to say that.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.680
Everyone has a good game face.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.810
Which one should I put in my deck?

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:53.400
Kirara has a draw skill that's 
valuable in a Nova Grappler deck.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.200
But I wanna conserve my Counterblasts,

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.800
so if I concentrate on power, 
would Eisenkugel be better?

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.260
How about Street Bouncer?

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.650
Street Bouncer?

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:12.940
Street Bouncer's skill is drawing if two 
cards are at rest in the rear-guard.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.640
I see! I can draw without 
using a Counterblast,

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.840
and it goes well with the skills of 
Top Gun and the Death Army units!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.880
This is the one to go with for sure!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.190
Thank you for the advice...

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.050
Kai!

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.120
You gave me advice?!

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.080
If you don't like it, don't 
take it. It's up to you.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.850
We're on the same team, so you 
could say it's only natural...

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:48.340
...but Kai has never done 
anything like that before.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:54.370
And no matter how right Kai was, Kamui would 
never do anything he says out of pride.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.570
I'll give this a try to see if 
it really is the best choice!

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.050
Let's fight, Kai!

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:09.560
Sure.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.370
To make the team stronger...

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.190
Vanguard <i>attack</i>!

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.720
What?! Intercept!

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.750
Stand up, the Vanguard!

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.750
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:31.160
You'll regret giving me advice after 
I give <i>you</i> a good walloping!

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.400
Say that <i>after</i> you win.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:39.390
Their back-and-forth is the same as 
before... and yet, it's completely different.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.450
Aichi, will you be my opponent?

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:46.070
I wanna try out the new deck I put together.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.830
Of course, Misaki.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.480
There's a nice atmosphere here.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.760
It looks like we've got the perfect balance 
for the finals tournament, too.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.980
I ride Stern Blaukluger!

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:21.320
Miss Emi, would you fight us?

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.280
WY... no?

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.300
Those voices!

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.590
Reiji? Eiji?

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:27.850
Please!

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.570
Th-Those guys...

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.620
Sure! Right?

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.470
Yeah!

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:38.010
Wha...?! No!!

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:39.030
Then let's go!

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.320
LG, LG!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:45.940
After everything I said, they're 
gonna ignore me and fight Miss Emi?!

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:50.350
Gloomy Gloomy Gloomy

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.470
I mean... naturally, they're gonna fight.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.330
Naturally... but still...

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.080
Rats!

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:57.710
Where are you going? We're 
in the middle of a fight.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:01.690
Th-They're planning to fight with my goddess!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:06.470
If you're a fighter, then act like 
one. Go <i>after</i> this match is over.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:11.330
Got it! I'm gonna beat you so 
fast it'll make your head spin!

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.190
Reiji! Eiji!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.440
If you beat Miss Emi, I'll make you pay!

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:28.090
I hate people who talk like that!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.380
Man, he's a busy guy.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.760
You're one to talk!

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:38.060
Let's fight fair and square!

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:38.650
Sure!

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.940
Why?! Why can't I be fighting Miss Emi?!

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:47.030
Why do I have to fight you?!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:51.060
It's, you know, ladycress!

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:54.260
Amusing, but you wanna say "ludicrous".

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.040
Don't turn Kai into a woman!

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:59.980
Right! Ladycrous!

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.460
Whatever.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.850
More importantly, focus on 
the fight in front of you.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.680
Shoot! Shoot, shoot!

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.100
Let's keep going here, too.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:21.610
Right!

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.770
Yeah!

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:36.600
After six turns, Emi has 5 damage...

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.290
Reiji has 3 damage!

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.460
I have to win during this turn!

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.670
I'm gonna protect myself so you <i>don't</i>!

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.880
It's my turn and I draw!

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.690
There it is! Here I go!

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.130
I ride Top Idol, Riviere!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.860
Ride?

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:57.390
Even though your Vanguard 
before, Top Idol, Serum

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.450
was also a grade 3 with 10000 power?

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:05.090
When Super Idol, Riviere is in the Soul,

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.170
Top Idol, Riviere gets +1000 power!

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.890
So that's why!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.210
I call Mermaid Idol, Felucca!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.800
I activate her skill! Soulcharge!

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:20.080
I attack with Pearl Sister, 
Perla, boosted by Perle!

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.350
No guard!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.140
Just 2 more...

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.640
I attack with Top Idol, Riviere!

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.100
I guard with Twin Blader!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.780
By dropping one card from my 
hand, I have perfect defense!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.800
Drive trigger check!

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.530
Draw trigger!

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:49.200
I add +5000 to the power 
of Top Idol, Pacifica!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.420
And then I draw!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.090
Second check!

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:10.760
Only Pacifica is left, and you 
need to do 2 more damage...

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:13.760
Pacifica's critical is 1...

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.800
It looks like I'm gonna win this match, huh?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.940
Nope! The match isn't over yet!

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:25.980
I attack with Pacifica, boosted by Felucca!

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:28.180
You're wasting your time. No guard!

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.140
Damage trigger check!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.740
5 damage... That's as far as it goes, huh?

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:45.780
Mai, it's okay!

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.120
When Pacifica's attack hits, 
her skill is activated!

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.010
Megablast!

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:04.310
I superior call three Bermuda Triangle 
units from my deck to the rear-guard!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.970
Flute! Sedna! Blazer Pleasures!

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:10.320
Perle and Perla exit the field!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.490
Flute's skill!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.670
When there are four or more Bermuda 
Triangle units in the rear-guard,

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:18.640
she receives +3000 power!

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:22.840
And then I activate Blazer 
Pleasures' skill!

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:27.480
When she enters the field, another Bermuda 
Triangle unit gets +2000 power!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.850
Of course, I give it to Flute!

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.990
I see! The units 
which have already attacked.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.290
They are replaced using superior call...?

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.010
With a boost from Sedna...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.180
...Flute attacks!

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.990
No guard!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:55.880
It's not over yet! DT, yo!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.740
D-Damage trigger check!

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.130
I lost.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.620
YL, yo.

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:06.410
Yay! Emi, that was fantastic!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.130
Junior Proof of Victory

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:13.010
Thank you! That was fun, Miss Emi!

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.410
TY, yo!

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.480
Finished!

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:26.480
The shop tournament...

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.170
...has come to a close!

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.690
Thank you, everyone!

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.380
The winner of the junior division is...

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.230
...Emi Sendou!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:44.730
Congratulations! To mark the occasion, 
you get Sub-manager's autograph!

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.120
Thank you!

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:48.630
Victory

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.660
Um...

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.900
Congratulations, Emi!

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.410
Congratulations!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.580
Emi...

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:59.300
Congratulations, Miss Emi! 
I knew you could do it!

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.990
N-Next time, I'll enter the junior division!

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:06.160
Thank you, Kamui!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.950
Happy ending, right, Kamui the Great?

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:10.400
HE, yo!

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.810
And the winner of the senior division is...

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.770
...Katsumi Morikawa!

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:21.710
Yeah!

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.550
I'm the strongest!

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.480
Great, Morikawa!

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:32.300
I guess I can't call him 
"Lose-umi" anymore...

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:38.080
I hate to admit it, but he's strong 
when he fights with a regular deck.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:43.380
Yay! Thank you!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:52.400
Since you defeated me, you have the 
right to call yourself "the strongest".

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:55.190
<i>Attack</i>...

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.880
What is this mood?

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.300
Was <i>he</i> really that strong?

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.740
<i>Attack</i>'s record...

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:07.380
Huh? He didn't even win once!

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:07.380
Osamu Kishida

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.900
Well, Morikawa, would you return that deck?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.560
Oh, that's right! Almost forgot!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.200
I've decided to buy this deck!

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.500
Thank you!

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:37.950
Even with this weak deck, I'm the strongest!

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.460
All I have to do...

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:44.910
...is improve it, and I can become 
the strongest of the strongest!

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.340
All right! I'll fix it as soon as I get home!

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.430
Fix it?

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:57.430
That means... that he...

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.780
I'm the strongest!

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:05.600
Morikawa is number one!

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:08.330
Number one! Number one! Number one!

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:16.000
Why? Why?!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.440
After all my wins yesterday, 
why can't I win today?!

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.810
I don't understand!

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:28.300
I customized the deck by putting 
in a bunch of grade 3s...

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.530
...so why am I not winning?!

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:40.330
This... This must be because 
I had a bad horoscope today!

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:42.950
Flower fortune, feng shui, and...

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.720
What should we do about him?

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:50.460
No! My strongest deck should be able to...

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:53.520
One more time! Fight me one more time!

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:56.430
This time for sure, I'll 
prove that I'm the strongest!

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.870
Morikawa...

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:01.190
I guess Morikawa will be Morikawa...

00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:04.310
I'm not sure if I feel 
disappointed or relieved...

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:05.030
You know?

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.490
Oh! You just laughed, didn't you, Kai?

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:10.800
Don't be stupid.

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.050
No, you laughed!

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.010
Shut up!

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:51.710
Why?!

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:53.470
I can't believe it!

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:55.820
My strongest grade 3 corps...!

00:23:55.820 --> 00:24:00.240
My goddess was right in front 
of me, but I couldn't fight her!

00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:01.360
Today's horoscope...

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:03.100
Yesterday's flower fortune...

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:04.620
The worst!

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:07.800
I forgot that fights were fun...

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.640
Thank you, everyone!

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:13.250
Next time: The Battle 
Begins! Tournament Finals.

00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:16.950
Fights with Team Caesar 
and Team AL4 are waiting.

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:19.720
My imagination will become my power!
